<figure id="A7.T13" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A7.T13.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A7.T13.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A7.T13.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A7.T13.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:455.2pt;">
<span id="A7.T13.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">You are a linguist proficient in various literary works.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A7.T13.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A7.T13.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A7.T13.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:455.2pt;">
<span id="A7.T13.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">Your current task is to determine whether the document and the question I provide are related. I will give you a document and a question. This question is a real user’s inquiry, and the document is content I have retrieved. The document may or may not be related to the question, so you need to make a judgment.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A7.T13.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A7.T13.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
