<tr id="A7.T16.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A7.T16.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A7.T16.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:455.2pt;">
<span id="A7.T16.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">I will give you several simple questions. Please combine them into a compound question. Since these questions are all about a certain entity, you need to follow the following rules:</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A7.T16.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A7.T16.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A7.T16.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:455.2pt;">
<span id="A7.T16.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">Rule 1: You need to fully understand the given questions and combine them perfectly;</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A7.T16.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A7.T16.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A7.T16.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:455.2pt;">
<span id="A7.T16.2.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">Rule 2: If the given questions cannot be combined, you only need to output "no";</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A7.T16.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A7.T16.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A7.T16.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:455.2pt;">
<span id="A7.T16.2.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">Rule 3: If they can be combined, the combined question must be a compound question, that is, this question must be about a certain entity and ask about several different aspects of the entity.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A7.T16.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A7.T16.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"></td></tr>
